    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d249">

                <pb facs="0247" n="237" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg237"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 E.W. 1939/9–1644: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-16T15:00:00+03:00">September 16,
                            1944—3 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 16—11:26 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3533. ReDeptel 2206, September 14, 9 p.m.<anchor n="31" xml:id="d249-f1"/>
                        Vyshinski,<anchor n="32" xml:id="d249-f2"/> the British Ambassador and I
                    yesterday signed on behalf of our respective <pb facs="0248" n="238"
                        xml:id="pg238"/> Governments the protocol to the Rumanian Armistice proposed
                    by the British. In addition to the two points reported in my 3423 of September
                    11, 2 p.m.,<anchor n="32a" xml:id="d249-f3"/> it contains a definition of war
                    material, reading, paraphrased, as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“In Article VII the term ‘material’ shall be deemed to include all
                            equipment or material belonging to, used by, or intended for use by,
                            enemy military or para-military formations or members thereof.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>The protocol is in the alternate form and is dated September 12 to coincide with
                    the date of the armistice. It will not be published.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harriman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
